  "caption": "Quinn's runner's knee came back again, even after hundreds of quad exercises. Rest, run, ouch, repeat.\n\nKay explained that the knee is often the victim, not the culprit: when hip control is weak, the knee can drift inward on every stride. Adding hip work to knee work tends to help more than knee work alone.\n\nWhat can help: glute training about three times a week for at least six weeks, slow step-downs with the knee over the toes, and building weekly running by no more than about 10%.\n\nGet it checked if your knee gives way or locks, pain follows a fall or knock, swelling lasts more than four weeks, or there's pain at rest, at night or with a fever.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
